(ABSTRACT) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 638 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 50 622 Tm
(This paper presents a comprehensive comparative analysis of deep learning architectures) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 606 Tm
(for medical image classification tasks. We evaluate Convolutional Neural Networks \(CNNs\),) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 590 Tm
(Vision Transformers \(ViTs\), and hybrid architectures across three benchmark medical) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 574 Tm
(imaging datasets: ChestX-ray14, ISIC 2019 \(dermoscopy\), and PathMNIST \(histopathology\).) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 558 Tm
(Our experiments demonstrate that hybrid CNN-Transformer models achieve state-of-the-art) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 542 Tm
(accuracy of 94.7 percent on chest X-ray classification while maintaining computational) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 526 Tm
(efficiency suitable for clinical deployment. We further propose an ensemble strategy) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 510 Tm
(combining ResNet-50, EfficientNet-B4, and Swin Transformer that yields a 2.3 percent) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 494 Tm
(improvement over individual model baselines. Statistical significance tests confirm the) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 478 Tm
(robustness of our findings across all evaluation metrics including AUC-ROC, F1-score, and) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 462 Tm
(sensitivity.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 446 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 50 430 Tm
/F1 13 Tf
(Keywords: Deep Learning, Medical Imaging, CNN, Vision Transformer, Transfer Learning, Classification) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 414 Tm
