1 0 0 1 50 398 Tm
/F1 13 Tf
(1. INTRODUCTION) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 382 Tm
(Medical image analysis has witnessed transformative advances through the application of) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 366 Tm
(deep learning techniques. Traditional computer-aided diagnosis systems relied heavily on) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 350 Tm
(handcrafted features and domain-specific preprocessing pipelines. The emergence of) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 334 Tm
(convolutional neural networks revolutionized this paradigm by enabling end-to-end feature) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 318 Tm
(learning directly from raw pixel data. Recent developments in attention mechanisms and) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 302 Tm
(transformer architectures have further expanded the methodological toolkit available to) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 286 Tm
(researchers. This study systematically compares these architectural families across) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 270 Tm
(standardized evaluation protocols.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 254 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 50 238 Tm
/F1 13 Tf
(2. RELATED WORK) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 222 Tm
(Prior work in medical image classification includes the seminal CheXNet architecture by) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 206 Tm
(Rajpurkar et al. which demonstrated radiologist-level performance on pneumonia detection.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 190 Tm
(Subsequent studies explored transfer learning from ImageNet-pretrained models, with) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 174 Tm
(DenseNet-121 and InceptionV3 emerging as popular backbone choices. The introduction of) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 158 Tm
(Vision Transformers by Dosovitskiy et al. opened new avenues for capturing global) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 142 Tm
(contextual information in medical images. Recent hybrid approaches such as TransMed and) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 126 Tm
(MedViT attempt to combine the inductive biases of CNNs with the long-range dependency) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 110 Tm
(modeling of transformers.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 94 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 50 78 Tm
/F1 13 Tf
